From d74412cf2a18f7d178bd6022495a1b85f642773b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 01:12:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Rated film Why drawer: Your rating, one prediction line,
 shown-scale verdicts, skeleton (rule 1820)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Owner-approved b76-rated-drawer-v2 ("Looks good, ship it"), web and iPhone, for a rated film:
- "Your rating" beside the stars, Share on the right.
- One prediction line under the stars: "We said N% before you watched · {verdict} ›" opening in
  place to the read we gave then (date, % at heading size, caveat); "We predicted N% · {verdict}"
  for a held-out guess; "We didn't predict this one" with none (matches on only). N is the shown %.
- Verdicts compare the shown % with the shown median at those stars (else DEFAULT_BY_STAR), on
  the server too (verdictFor, expectedByStar, shownVerdict; match-csv predictedVerdict). Words:
  Spot on / We undersold it / We overshot it, also in Called it, Spot on, the guess line, saidLine.
- The "What we'd have predicted" box is gone; "Closest in your films" on rated films.
- The film page card uses the same saved-then-held-out guess and never the stored match.
- A skeleton for the rated drawer in the loaded layout.
Rules 427, 446, 454, 535, 645, 989, 1069, 1084, 1097, 1183, 1189, 1279, 1290, 1382, 1415, 1512,
1531, 1545, 1598 amended; DATA-SCIENCE-LOG entry. iPhone not compiled here.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013WRDCFXH8nihP92apJAVW7
