-1545. **Match scores are judged on what a person rates next; the share cap made safe; a rated film shows the held-out number** (owner 2026-11-12: "predict what people will like in the future, not fit their past"; test and report: mockups/journeys/match-time-split.md, scripts/eval-time-split/; amends 1488 and 645). (1) The test for any change to match scores is the time split: fit on a person's earlier ratings, score their later ones (their last ~20% by date, and one global cutoff date); a random hold-out is a secondary check only. A change ships only if per-user Spearman and AUC for 4.5★+ do not fall beyond noise (bootstrap over users), the shown bands stay ordered with a higher band accuracy, and more held-out 5★ films show 85% or more. (2) The model 9 share cap (rule 1488) is safe on thin libraries (`V9_CAP_FIX`, lib/taste/match-model.mjs): a person's own fit is capped only from `V9_SHARE_MIN_RATED` (100) rated films, below that it is the fit from the already-capped population prior; the shares are read on the unshrunk normalised features, so the cold-start shrink (rule 1080) is not undone; a group with under `V9_SHARE_MIN_MASS` of the total movement is left alone; no personal group grows by more than `V9_SHARE_MAX_FACTOR` (2), the crowd and 'other' coming down further instead so their caps (30% since 2026-11-12, rule 1488 as amended; 20% before; and 5%) still hold. No weight may exceed 10 (the old cap sent a 13-rating account's Film DNA weights to 4e15 and ran its order backwards). `MATCH_V9_CAPFIX=off` restores the old cap for evals only. `FULL_PASS.CATALOG_FIXED_AT` moved to 2026-11-12 02:00 UTC, so the match-scores cron refits and rescores everyone once; nothing is written by hand. (3) A rated film never shows its stored score, which was fitted with the film's own rating in it: the web Prediction card reads the guess shown before the rating, else the held-out one (`res.predictedMatch`, the film left out), else the stored match, as the iPhone already does (`said ?? fresh ?? predictedBefore ?? match`). Checked by `scripts/check-invariants.ts` (1545) and `scripts/test-match-v9.ts`.
